   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The relation gives \\( f'(-1) = -1 \\). Differentiate the relation, using the product rule and the chain rule on each term that holds \\( f \\): \\( f'' = f^{2} + 2 f f' x \\).",
         "mathjson": -1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Evaluate in order at \\( x = -1 \\), feeding each value into the next: \\( f'(-1) = -1 \\), \\( f''(-1) = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Divide each value by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{1}{0!} = 1 \\), \\( \\frac{-1}{1!} = -1 \\), \\( \\frac{3}{2!} = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
